  "question": "What does Part 5.2 require, and which of our own documents shows that we actually do it?",
  "answer": "I have reviewed the text for **CIP-007-6 Part 5.2**, which is part of the \"System Access Controls\" table (Table R5).\n\nThis specific part of the requirement mandates that for High Impact and certain Medium Impact BES Cyber Systems, the Responsible Entity must **identify and inventory all known enabled default or other generic account types**. This inventory can be organized by system, groups of systems, location, or system type [csection-ec458b69bb605a5c345a].\n\nThe standard provides an example of evidence for this duty, which includes a listing of accounts by account types that explicitly shows which enabled or generic accounts are currently in use [csection-ec458b69bb605a5c345a].\n\nI have not yet reviewed any of the operator's internal procedures or notes to see how they perform this inventory or if they have established a more stringent requirement (for example, a specific frequency for the inventory or a different method of organization).\n\nCited sections:\n- csection-ec458b69bb605a5c345a (CIP-007-6 R5 Part 5.2 requirement and measure)",
